{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a08f75-0d33-79f3-abbb-fac7df226d36","session_id":"01a08f74-c077-7bd3-8de8-2cfab5bccb52","message":{"id":"01a08f750d3379f3abbbfac59de79fa5","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The catalog in cli.py (line 265) checks the *package manifest* against EXPECTED_CLI_CATALOG — not the actual parser. Let me check that. Line 265 is inside `_package_verify` presumably. So EXPECTED_CLI_CATALOG is a contract for the package manifest. Adding a new CLI subcommand doesn't require changing EXPECTED_CLI_CATALOG (and the whitelist says only add the subcommand, don't touch other code). But wait — is there a test that asserts the actual argparse parser matches EXPECTED_CLI_CATALOG? Let me check package-manifest.json's cli.catalog and test_cli_help.py.\n\nActually the whitelist is strict: \"修改 src/ci_workflow/cli.py（仅新增 research fetch-pubmed 子命令，不动其他代码）\". So I must NOT add to EXPECTED_CLI_CATALOG. Good — that's fine as long as nothing cross-checks the parser against the catalog. Let me verify with a quick grep for tests that enumerate the parser.\n\nLet me check test_cli_help.py.","signature":""}],"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","role":"assistant","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"input_tokens":0,"output_tokens":0,"cache_creation_input_tokens":null,"cache_read_input_tokens":null,"cache_creation":null,"server_tool_use":null,"service_tier":null}},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a08f74c0e77b339467e8764f913e8f","_messageId":"01a08f750d3379f3abbbfac59de79fa5","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a08f74c0e77b339467e8764f913e8f","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a08f750d3379f3abbbfac59de79fa5","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a08f750d3379f3abbbfac59de79fa5","codebuddy.ai/messageId":"01a08f75-0d33-79f3-abbb-fac7df226d36","traceparent":"00-ad7bdc66d5296f999aa4edc599e201ac-2aad9b60b4e08bab-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a08f74-c077-7bd3-8de8-2cfab5bccb52,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a08f74c0e77b339467