{"type":"user","uuid":"01a08f75-8b42-70a2-83ed-bed377f840be","session_id":"01a08f74-c077-7bd3-8de8-2cfab5bccb52","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_00_5xCQ5ghHMimXbhgFfdk01935","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→Delegated mode（执行模块角色：Worker-C，有界执行）\n   2→\n   3→# 硬边界\n   4→\n   5→1. 唯一工作区：/Users/smkzw/Documents/AI Products/competitive-intelligence-workflow。禁止访问路径含\"竞品调研工作流\"的旧中文工程。\n   6→2. 允许写入的文件（严格白名单，其他一律不碰）：\n   7→   - 新建 src/ci_workflow/sources/connectors/pubmed_fetch.py\n   8→   - 新建 tests/integration/sources/test_pubmed_fetch.py\n   9→   - 修改 src/ci_workflow/cli.py（仅新增 research fetch-pubmed 子命令，不动其他代码）\n  10→   - 新建 packets/2026-09-11-p2-routes/runs/worker-c-report.md（你的输出报告）\n  11→3. 禁止：git 任何写操作（add/commit/restore/clean）、修改本清单外任何文件、运行会写仓库的命令（uv run pytest 只允许跑你自己的新测试文件）、访问网络（测试全部用合成 transport，不真连 PubMed）。\n  12→4. 不声称最终验收；派发方持有验收。\n  13→\n  14→# 任务：PubMed 真实获取路线（仿 CT.gov 模式）\n  15→\n  16→先读这三个文件作为模式范本：\n  17→- src/ci_workflow/sources/connectors/ctgov_fetch.py（获取器范本：stdlib-only、禁重定向 opener、超时/限流/坏响应分类、CAS 原始字节保存、游标/预算、失败不冒充无数据）\n  18→- src/ci_workflow/sources/connectors/pubmed.py（已有的 URL 构造 :104 与 XML 解析 :125，复用它们，不要重写）\n  19→- src/ci_workflow/cli.py 中 _research_fetch_ctgov_handler（CLI 接法范本）\n  20→\n  21→实现：\n  22→1. pubmed_fetch.py：`fetch_pubmed_results(query/term, ...)`，复用 pubmed.py 的 URL 构造与 XML 解析；要求：\n  23→   - stdlib only（urllib.request，自定义 opener 禁 redirect）\n  24→   - 区分超时/HTTP 错误/限流(429)/坏 XML/空结果，各自抛不同异常类型，绝不把失败当\"无结果\"\n  25→   - 原始响应字节写入 ContentAddressedStore（照抄 ctgov_fetch 的用法），返回带 CAS 指针的回执 dataclass\n  26→   - 回执含：query、总数、条数、原始字节 sha256、CAS 相对路径、获取时刻 UTC、`universe_closed: Literal[False]`、`temporal_scope: \"current_records\"`（与 ctgov 同样的诚实限制字段）\n  27→2. cli.py：`research fetch-pubmed --term <词> --root <项目或输出目录>`，行为对齐 fetch-ctgov（输出精简 JSON 指针，不回显正文）\n  28→3. tests/integration/sources/test_pubmed_fetch.py：全部合成 transport（monkeypatch urllib/opener），覆盖：正常两页分页（retstart/retmax 游标）、429 限流、超时、坏 XML、空结果集、重复游标死循环保护、CAS 字节写入与 sha 一致、CLI 入口参数校验。先写测试看它失败，再实现。\n  29→\n  30→# 验证命令（只许跑你自己的）\n  31→\n  32→uv run pytest tests/integration/sources/test_pubmed_fetch.py -q --tb=short\n  33→uv run ruff check src/ci_workflow/sources/connectors/pubmed_fetch.py\n  34→uv run python -m mypy --no-incremental --strict src/ci_workflow/sources/connectors/pubmed_fetch.py\n  35→\n  36→# 输出报告（worker-c-report.md，Markdown）\n  37→\n  38→## 结果\n  39→完成/未完成一句话。\n  40→## 变更清单\n  41→逐文件：新建/修改 + 行数 + 关键函数签名。\n  42→## 测试证据\n  43→命令 + 通过数（贴尾行）。\n  44→## 设计说明\n  45→与 ctgov_fetch 的差异点；复用了 pubmed.py 哪些函数。\n  46→## 未验证项\n  47→如实列出（如：真实网络未测）。\n  48→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a08f74c0e77b339467e8764f913e8f","_messageId":"01a08f7582be7b4fbede7d13666011b4","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a08f74c0e77b339467e8764f913e8f","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a08f7582be7b4fbede7d13666011b4","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a08f7582be7b4fbede7d13666011b4","traceparent":"00-ad7bdc66d5296f999aa4edc599e201ac-2aad9b60b4e08bab-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a08f74-c077-7bd3-8de8-2cfab5bccb52,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a08f74c0e77b339467e8764f913e8f"},"__timestamp":"2026-09-11T07:54:00.387Z"}
{"type":"user","uuid":"01a08f75-8b44-72fc-89d5-3214e629afcc","session_id":"01a08f74-c077-7bd3-8de8-2cfab5bccb52","message":{"content":[{"type":"tool_result","tool_use_id":"call_01_jPvmIFnl0sTbFsFfmF900550","content":[{"type":"text","text":"   1→# Quality Guidelines\n   2→\n   3→> Code quality standards for backend development.\n   4→\n   5→---\n   6→\n   7→## Overview\n   8→\n   9→Backend acceptance is fail-closed for evidence-to-report transformations. A green\n  10→model constructor is not an integrity proof when later code can receive Pydantic\n  11→instances produced by `model_copy(update=...)`.\n  12→\n  13→---\n  14→\n  15→## Forbidden Patterns\n  16→\n  17→- Do not export a constructor/aggregator pair that accepts detached evaluated\n  18→  results and stamps a new evidence snapshot or rule fingerprint onto them.\n  19→- Do not trust `frozen=True` or construction-time validators at an authoritative\n  20→  aggregation boundary; `model_copy(update=...)` does not re-run validation.\n  21→- Do not accept report-gate results without independently deriving the complete\n  22→  `(unit_id, object_id)` matrix from the current `GateSpec` and closed universe.\n  23→\n  24→---\n  25→\n  26→## Required Patterns\n  27→\n  28→- Public evaluation must be atomic: current rule + current closed snapshot +\n  29→  current fact bindings go in; one immutable report result comes out.\n  30→- Internal aggregate boundaries must re-derive content digests and identity keys\n  31→  from the instance's current serialized content before semantic aggregation.\n  32→- Rule content fingerprints, evidence snapshot identifiers, universe summaries,\n  33→  and distinct immutable fact lineage must all participate in validation.\n  34→\n  35→---\n  36→\n  37→## Testing Requirements\n  38→\n  39→- Every authoritative Pydantic boundary needs a `model_copy` adversarial test.\n  40→- Changed-snapshot and same-version changed-rule tests must prove recomputation,\n  41→  not only key inequality.\n  42→- Public-surface tests must verify unsupported detached constructors are absent,\n  43→  while production call-site search verifies there is no alternate supported path.\n  44→\n  45→---\n  46→\n  47→## Code Review Checklist\n  48→\n  49→- Does any public path accept pre-evaluated unit results?\n  50→- Does aggregation revalidate current content before reading semantic fields?\n  51→- Are thresholds and the complete object matrix derived from the current spec?\n  52→- Do parent results remain immutable during project-rule recomputation?\n  53→- Do exact attacks, full regression, lint, strict typing, and package verification pass?\n  54→\n  55→## Scenario: Atomic evidence evaluation and batch-integrity revalidation\n  56→\n  57→### 1. Scope / Trigger\n  58→\n  59→- Trigger: adding or changing a gate evaluator, report result loader, evidence\n  60→  snapshot, project-rule override, or any intermediate Pydantic batch used before\n  61→  report acceptance.\n  62→- Prevents: stale unit results being re-stamped under a new snapshot or changed\n  63→  rule, and unvalidated `model_copy` mutations producing a false pass.\n  64→\n  65→### 2. Signatures\n  66→\n  67→Supported public evaluation signature:\n  68→\n  69→```python\n  70→def evaluate_report(\n  71→    spec: GateSpec,\n  72→    snapshot: ApplicableUniverseSnapshot,\n  73→    bindings: Sequence[GateEvidenceBinding],\n  74→    *,\n  75→    contract_version: str,\n  76→) -> ReportGateResult: ...\n  77→```\n  78→\n  79→Internal-only aggregation shape:\n  80→\n  81→```python\n  82→def _aggregate_report_gates(\n  83→    *,\n  84→    spec: GateSpec,\n  85→    snapshot: ApplicableUniverseSnapshot,\n  86→    batch: _GateEvaluationBatch,\n  87→    contract_version: str,\n  88→) -> ReportGateResult: ...\n  89→```\n  90→\n  91→`_GateEvaluationBatch`, `_aggregate_report_gates`, batch-key helpers, and detached\n  92→unit-result construction are not package-root exports.\n  93→\n  94→### 3. Contracts\n  95→\n  96→- `spec.spec_fingerprint` identifies rule content, not only version text.\n  97→- `snapshot` must be closed and carries `evidence_snapshot_id` and\n  98→  `universe_summary`.\n  99→- `batch_key` is derived from report kind, snapshot identifier, universe summary,\n 100→  rule fingerprint, and the ordered canonical digest of all unit results.\n 101→- The authoritative output derives identity from the current `spec` and\n 102→  `snapshot`; callers cannot supply replacement identity strings.\n 103→\n 104→### 4. Validation & Error Matrix\n 105→\n 106→| Condition | Required behavior |\n 107→|---|---|\n 108→| Forged batch key via `model_copy` | Raise `GateEvaluationError` before aggregation |\n 109→| Nested unit result changed without matching original key | Raise `GateEvaluationError` before aggregation |\n 110→| Batch snapshot differs from current snapshot | Reject as snapshot mismatch |\n 111→| Batch rule fingerprint differs from current spec | Reject as rule mismatch |\n 112→| Missing or extra `(unit_id, object_id)` result | Reject as incomplete matrix |\n 113→| Same-version rule raises threshold | Re-evaluate bindings; block when count is insufficient |\n 114→| New snapshot with the same object IDs | Re-evaluate and emit a new snapshot-bound result |\n 115→\n 116→### 5. Good / Base / Bad Cases\n 117→\n 118→- Good: `evaluate_report(current_spec, current_snapshot, current_bindings, ...)`\n 119→  evaluates units and aggregates in one call.\n 120→- Base: repeating the call with unchanged inputs yields the same deterministic\n 121→  result identity.\n 122→- Bad: constructing results under A, then asking an exported helper to stamp them\n 123→  as B. No supported public helper may provide this behavior.\n 124→- Bad: relying on `frozen=True` after `batch.model_copy(update=...)`.\n 125→\n 126→### 6. Tests Required\n 127→\n 128→- `test_aggregate_rejects_model_copy_tampered_batch_key_or_unit_results`\n 129→  asserts a valid internal batch passes, forged key and nested lineage changes\n 130→  fail, and the source batch bytes stay unchanged.\n 131→- `test_public_batch_constructor_rejects_detached_unit_results_from_changed_snapshot_or_spec`\n 132→  asserts the detached API is absent and public evaluation recomputes for a new\n 133→  snapshot and raised same-version threshold.\n 134→- Exact report-gate, report-specific, and override suites must remain green with\n 135→  the full repository regression.\n 136→\n 137→### 7. Wrong vs Correct\n 138→\n 139→#### Wrong\n 140→\n 141→```python\n 142→old_results = evaluate_units(spec_a, snapshot_a, bindings)\n 143→batch_b = PublicBatch.from_evaluation(spec_b, snapshot_b, old_results)\n 144→return public_aggregate(spec_b, snapshot_b, batch_b)\n 145→```\n 146→\n 147→#### Correct\n 148→\n 149→```python\n 150→return evaluate_report(\n 151→    spec_b,\n 152→    snapshot_b,\n 153→    bindings,\n 154→    contract_version=contract_version,\n 155→)\n 156→```\n 157→"}],"is_error":false}],"role":"user"},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"_requestId":"01a08f74c0e77b339467e8764f913e8f","_messageId":"01a08f7582be7b4fbede7d13666011b4","_meta":{"codebuddy.ai/conversationRequestId":"01a08f74c0e77b339467e8764f913e8f","codebuddy.ai/modelRequestId":"01a08f7582be7b4fbede7d13666011b4","codebuddy.ai/llmMessageId":"01a08f7582be7b4fbede7d13666011b4","traceparent":"00-ad7bdc66d5296f999aa4edc599e201ac-2aad9b60b4e08bab-01","baggage":"codebuddy.session_id=01a08f74-c077-7bd3-8de8-2cfab5bccb52,codebuddy.conversation_request_id=01a08f74c0e77b339467e8764f913e8f"},"__timestamp":"2026-09-11T07:54:00.388Z"}
{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a08f75-8b4f-7cfe-b2f3-e6baf0585eb8","session_id":"01a08f74-c077-7bd3-8de8-2cfab5bccb52","message":{"id":"01a08f758b4f7cfeb2f3e6b87e08ab05","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now let me check the existing pubmed cross-reference test to see the existing patterns for pubmed, and check whether there is an efetch URL builder elsewhere. Let me also check `test_pubmed_cross_reference.py`.\n\nAlso, I should check the domain/evidence.py ContentBlob definition.\n\nLet me now decide the design concretely.\n\n### pubmed_fetch.py design\n\n```python\n\"\"\"Bounded PubMed E-utilities acquisition; pagination is not evidence completeness.\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport json\nfrom collections.abc import Callable\nfrom dataclasses import dataclass\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Literal, Protocol\nfrom urllib.error import HTTPError, URLError\nfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs, urlencode, urlsplit, urlunsplit\nfrom urllib.request import HTTPRedirectHandler, Request, build_opener\n\nfrom pydantic import BaseModel, ConfigDict\n\nfrom ci_workflow.domain.evidence import ContentBlob\nfrom ci_workflow.sources.connectors.pubmed import (\n    PubMedRecord,\n    build_pubmed_nct_search_url,\n    parse_pubmed_efetch_xml,\n)\nfrom ci_workflow.storage.content_store import ContentAddressedStore\n\nEUTILS_ROOT = ...\n```\n\nHmm — how to reuse the URL construction. Let me write:\n\n```python\n_SEARCH = urlsplit(build_pubmed_nct_search_url(\"NCT00000001\"))\n_ESEARCH_ENDPOINT = urlunsplit((_SEARCH.scheme, _SEARCH.netloc, _SEARCH.path, \"\", \"\"))\n```\nThat gives \"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi\". And base params db=pubmed, retmode=json from `parse_qs(_SEARCH.query)`.\n\nThen:\n```python\ndef build_pubmed_term_search_url(term: str, *, retstart: int, retmax: int) -> str:\n    base = {key: values[0] for key, values in parse_qs(_SEARCH.query).items()}\n    base.pop(\"term\", None)\n    base.update({\"term\": term, \"retstart\": str(retstart), \"retmax\": str(retmax)})\n    return f\"{_ESEARCH_ENDPOINT}?{urlencode(base)}\"\n```\nHmm, but a module-level call to a function that validates NCT and raises is fine (constant is valid). But wait: does this look like a hack a reviewer would reject? It's defensible but a bit indirect. Let me think about whether there's a more natural option.\n\nActually — hmm, maybe I should reconsider: perhaps reuse `build_pubmed_nct_search_url` for real, for the NCT-anchored route, and make the primary public function term-based. The task's receipt wants \"query\" — free text is fine.\n\nHonest approach: I'll implement `build_pubmed_term_search_url` derived from the reused builder's endpoint and base params, with a comment explaining that pubmed.py owns the canonical endpoint/db/retmode and this module only supplies term/pagination. That satisfies \"复用 URL 构造，不要重写\" reasonably: no duplicated host/path literals.\n\nHmm, wait. Actually there's a real risk: mypy strict + `parse_qs` returns `dict[str, list[str]]`. Fine.\n\nHmm, one more consideration: maybe simpler and more robust — reuse `build_pubmed_nct_search_url` directly when the term is an NCT id, so the NCT route is byte-identical to pubmed.py's canonical URL (term=f\"{nct}[All Fields]\", retmode=json, retmax=10000). But retmax=10000 breaks paging. I'd have to override retmax anyway. So the derived-endpoint approach is uniform. Let me just do the derived endpoint, and additionally assert in tests that the term URL starts with the same endpoint as pubmed.py's builder.\n\nHmm, hold on. Let me reconsider the whole \"reuse\" thing once more. Is there a chance the dispatcher wants me to NOT add a URL builder but instead call `build_pubmed_nct_search_url` and then swap params? That's basically what I'm doing. OK. Go.\n\n### Two-phase fetch\n\nPhase A: esearch pagination (JSON).\nPhase B: efetch (XML) for the collected PMIDs.\n\nBut hmm — for the receipt, which raw bytes go to CAS? Both. `pages: tuple[CapturedPage, ...]` for esearch pages and `records_page` for efetch XML? Let me design the receipt to mirror ctgov:\n\n```python\nclass CapturedPage(BaseModel):   # esearch page\n    page_number: int\n    request_url: str\n    acquired_at: datetime\n    raw_asset: ContentBlob\n    pmids: tuple[str, ...]\n\nclass PubMedFetchResult(BaseModel):\n    query: str\n    status: FetchStatus\n    pagination_complete: bool\n    universe_closed: Literal[False] = False\n    temporal_scope: Literal[\"current_records\"] = \"current_records\"\n    total_count: int | None\n    records: tuple[PubMedRecord, ...]\n    pages: tuple[CapturedPage, ...]\n    records_asset: ContentBlob | None\n    diagnostic: str\n```\n\nHmm, the task says \"回执含：query、总数、条数、原始字节 sha256、CAS 相对路径、获取时刻 UTC、universe_closed: Literal[False]、temporal_scope\". \"条数\" = record count. Note: \"原始字节 sha256 / CAS 相对路径\" — could be satisfied by the ContentBlob objects (which carry sha256 + relative_path). And \"获取时刻 UTC\" by acquired_at.\n\nHmm, the task says \"返回带 CAS 指针的回执 dataclass\". dataclass or pydantic model? ctgov uses pydantic BaseModel (which is not a dataclass). The spec says \"dataclass\" loosely. I'll use pydantic BaseModel to match ctgov (it's the project pattern), and note it. Hmm — \"返回带 CAS 指针的回执 dataclass\" — a pydantic model is fine; the CLI needs model_dump(mode=\"json\"). I'll use pydantic to stay consistent with ctgov_fetch, and mention it in the report.\n\nHmm, but strictly \"dataclass\" was requested... Using `@dataclass(frozen=True)` for the receipt would be inconsistent with ctgov's `CtgovFetchResult` and would break `.model_dump()`. The \"行为对齐 fetch-ctgov\" instruction is stronger. I'll use pydantic and document.\n\nHmm, actually, wait. Let me re-read: \"原始响应字节写入 ContentAddressedStore（照抄 ctgov_fetch 的用法），返回带 CAS 指针的回执 dataclass\". \"照抄 ctgov_fetch 的用法\" — ctgov uses pydantic BaseModel for the result. I'll go pydantic. Document in 设计说明.\n\n### Failure taxonomy and statuses\n\nMirror ctgov statuses:\n- `network_error`: timeout/URLError/OSError\n- `rate_limited`: 429\n- `access_denied`: 401/403\n- `invalid_response`: redirect, non-200, wrong content type, bad JSON/XML, missing fields\n- `incomplete`: budget exhausted, duplicate cursor, count drift, record count mismatch\n- `no_records`: authoritative empty\n- `complete`\n\nDistinct exception types (internal, raised by helpers, exported):\n```python\nclass PubMedFetchError(RuntimeError): ...\nclass PubMedTimeoutError(PubMedFetchError)      # timeout\nclass PubMedNetworkError(PubMedFetchError)      # connection/OSError\nclass PubMedRateLimitedError(PubMedFetchError)  # 429\nclass PubMedHttpError(PubMedFetchError)         # other HTTP status (403/500/...)\nclass PubMedMalformedResponseError(PubMedFetchError)  # bad XML/JSON/redirect/content-type\nclass PubMedEmptyResultError(PubMedFetchError)  # authoritative zero records\n```\nAnd `fetch_pubmed_results` catches `PubMedFetchError` subclasses → maps to status. This gives \"各自抛不同异常类型\" literally at the helper boundary and \"失败不冒充无数据\" at the receipt boundary.\n\nHmm, is that satisfying? The spec bullet says \"区分超时/HTTP 错误/限流(429)/坏 XML/空结果，各自抛不同异常类型\". I'll make the helpers raise these and document. I think the hybrid is right, and the tests will assert:\n- helper raises distinct types for each fault\n- fetch_pubmed_results maps each to distinct status, never \"no_records\"\n\nThat's stronger evidence than either alone. \n\nWait, but there's a risk the reviewer wants the public function to raise. Hmm. Given ctgov precedent (which the prompt says to copy: \"失败不冒充无数据\" via status) and the CLI alignment requirement, returning statuses is right. And the receipt is only returned when... hmm, actually on failure ctgov returns a receipt with empty pages. Fine.\n\nHmm, actually, hmm. Let me reconsider: should `fetch_pubmed_results` raise on failure and the CLI catch? Let's look at what the CLI test needs: \"CLI 入口参数校验\