{"type":"assistant","uuid":"01a08f76-fbdc-7571-8256-e345c588a0d9","session_id":"01a08f74-c077-7bd3-8de8-2cfab5bccb52","message":{"id":"01a08f76fbdc75718256e343dea8b362","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now write the test file. Let me be careful with mypy? The verification only runs mypy on the source file, and ruff only on pubmed_fetch.py. Tests just need to run under pytest.\n\nLet me write the tests now.\n\nTest file content:\n\n```python\n\"\"\"PubMed acquisition evidence: pagination, failure kinds and raw-byte custody.\n\nEvery transport here is synthetic; no test reaches the network.\n\"\"\"\n\nfrom __future__ import annotations\n\nimport hashlib\nimport json\nfrom datetime import UTC, datetime, timedelta\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom urllib.error import HTTPError, URLError\nfrom urllib.parse import parse_qs, urlsplit\n\nimport pytest\n\nfrom ci_workflow.cli import main\nfrom ci_workflow.sources.connectors import pubmed_fetch\nfrom ci_workflow.sources.connectors.pubmed_fetch import (\n    HttpPage,\n    PubMedAccessDeniedError,\n    PubMedNetworkError,\n    PubMedRateLimitedError,\n    PubMedServerError,\n    PubMedTimeoutError,\n    fetch_pubmed_results,\n)\nfrom ci_workflow.storage.content_store import ContentAddressedStore\nfrom tests.integration.test_research_package_submission import _project\n\nNOW = datetime(2026, 9, 11, 3, 0, tzinfo=UTC)\n\n\ndef _clock() -> datetime:\n    return NOW\n\n\nclass Pages:\n    \"\"\"Synthetic E-utilities transport: queued bytes, HttpPage, or raised exception.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self, items: list[bytes | HttpPage | Exception]) -> None:\n        self.items = iter(items)\n        self.urls: list[str] = []\n\n    def __call__(self, url: str, timeout: float, max_bytes: int) -> HttpPage:\n        self.urls.append(url)\n        value = next(self.items)\n        if isinstance(value, Exception):\n            raise value\n        if isinstance(value, HttpPage):\n            return value\n        media_type = \"application/json\" if \"esearch.fcgi\" in url else \"text/xml\"\n        return HttpPage(200, media_type, value, url)\n\n\ndef _search_page(count: int, retstart: int, retmax: int, ids: list[str]) -> bytes:\n    return json.dumps({\n        \"header\": {\"type\": \"esearch\"},\n        \"esearchresult\": {\n            \"count\": str(count), \"retstart\": str(retstart), \"retmax\": str(retmax), \"idlist\": ids,\n        },\n    }).encode(\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef _article(pmid: str) -> str:\n    return (\n        \"<PubmedArticle><MedlineCitation>\"\n        f\"<PMID>{pmid}</PMID><Article><ArticleTitle>合成题名{pmid}</ArticleTitle>\"\n        \"<Abstract><AbstractText>合成摘要内容</AbstractText></Abstract>\"\n        \"<PublicationTypeList><PublicationType>Randomized Controlled Trial</PublicationType>\"\n        \"</PublicationTypeList></Article></MedlineCitation></PubmedArticle>\"\n    )\n\n\ndef _records_xml(*pmids: str) -> bytes:\n    body = \"\".join(_article(pmid) for pmid in pmids)\n    return f'<?xml version=\"1.0\"?><PubmedArticleSet>{body}</PubmedArticleSet>'.encode(\"utf-8\")\n\n\ndef _fetch(tmp_path, pages, **overrides):  # helper? maybe not needed\n```\n\nHmm, `fetch_pubmed_results(project_root, query, *, page_size=..., ...)`. Signature: positional (project_root, query). Let me define signature:\n\n```python\ndef fetch_pubmed_results(\n    project_root: Path,\n    query: str,\n    *,\n    page_size: int = 200,\n    max_pages: int = 1000,\n    timeout: float = 30,\n    max_page_bytes: int = 20 * 1024 * 1024,\n    max_total_bytes: int = 128 * 1024 * 1024,\n    efetch_batch_size: int = 200,\n    transport: Transport | None = None,\n    clock: Callable[[], datetime] = lambda: datetime.now(UTC),\n) -> PubMedFetchResult:\n```\n\nNow tests. Let me write them.\n\nTest 1: two-page search then fetch.\n\n```python\ndef test_two_page_search_keeps_cursor_and_exact_raw_bytes(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([\n        _search_page(2, 0, 1, [\"111\"]),\n        _search_page(2, 1, 1, [\"222\"]),\n        _records_xml(\"111\", \"222\"),\n    ])\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(\n        tmp_path, \"pembrolizumab AND NSCLC\", page_size=1, transport=pages, clock=_clock,\n    )\n    assert result.status == \"complete\" and result.pagination_complete\n    assert result.total_count == 2\n    assert [record.pmid for record in result.records] == [\"111\", \"222\"]\n    assert result.acquired_at == NOW and result.acquired_at.utcoffset() == timedelta(0)\n    assert result.universe_closed is False and result.temporal_scope == \"current_records\"\n    assert len(result.search_pages) == 2 and len(result.record_pages) == 1\n\n    first = parse_qs(urlsplit(pages.urls[0]).query)\n    second = parse_qs(urlsplit(pages.urls[1]).query)\n    assert first[\"term\"] == [\"pembrolizumab AND NSCLC\"]\n    assert (first[\"retstart\"], first[\"retmax\"]) == ([\"0\"], [\"1\"])\n    assert (second[\"retstart\"], second[\"retmax\"]) == ([\"1\"], [\"1\"])\n    assert parse_qs(urlsplit(pages.urls[2]).query)[\"id\"] == [\"111,222\"]\n\n    store = ContentAddressedStore(tmp_path)\n    for page, body in zip((*result.search_pages, *result.record_pages),\n                          (_search_page(2, 0, 1, [\"111\"]), _search_page(2, 1, 1, [\"222\"]),\n                           _records_xml(\"111\", \"222\")), strict=True):\n        raw = store.read_bytes(page.raw_asset)\n        assert raw == body\n        assert hashlib.sha256(raw).hexdigest() == page.raw_asset.sha256\n        assert page.raw_asset.relative_path == (\n            f\"evidence/raw/sha256/{page.raw_asset.sha256[:2]}/{page.raw_asset.sha256}.bin\"\n        )\n        assert page.acquired_at == NOW\n```\n\nNote `zip(..., strict=True)` — Python 3.12 ok.\n\nHmm, `result.search_pages` type is tuple[CapturedResponse, ...].\n\nTest: efetch chunking.\n\n```python\ndef test_records_are_fetched_in_bounded_chunks(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([\n        _search_page(2, 0, 2, [\"111\", \"222\"]),\n        _records_xml(\"111\"),\n        _records_xml(\"222\"),\n    ])\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", efetch_batch_size=1, transport=pages, clock=_clock)\n    assert result.status == \"complete\"\n    assert [record.pmid for record in result.records] == [\"111\", \"222\"]\n    assert len(result.record_pages) == 2\n    assert parse_qs(urlsplit(pages.urls[1]).query)[\"id\"] == [\"111\"]\n    assert parse_qs(urlsplit(pages.urls[2]).query)[\"id\"] == [\"222\"]\n```\n\nTest: failures.\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize((\"failure\", \"expected\"), [\n    (TimeoutError(\"timed out\"), \"network_error\"),\n    (URLError(\"connection refused\"), \"network_error\"),\n    (HttpPage(429, \"\", b\"\", \"\"), \"rate_limited\"),\n    (HttpPage(403, \"\", b\"\", \"\"), \"access_denied\"),\n    (HttpPage(503, \"\", b\"\", \"\"), \"network_error\"),\n    (HttpPage(302, \"\", b\"\", \"\"), \"invalid_response\"),\n    (b\"<html>not json</html>\", \"invalid_response\"),\n    (b'{\"esearchresult\":{\"count\":\"3\",\"retstart\":\"0\",\"retmax\":\"3\",\"idlist\":[],\"ERROR\":\"Invalid term\"}}', \"invalid_response\"),\n])\ndef test_every_failure_kind_stays_distinct_from_no_records(\n    tmp_path: Path, failure: bytes | HttpPage | Exception, expected: str,\n) -> None:\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", transport=Pages([failure]), clock=_clock)\n    assert result.status == expected\n    assert not result.pagination_complete\n    assert result.records == () and result.total_count is None\n    assert result.universe_closed is False\n    assert not (tmp_path / \"evidence\").exists()\n```\n\nHmm, wait: HttpPage(302,...) with final_url \"\" — my orchestrator: `_raise_for_status(302)` → PubMedHttpError → invalid_response. OK. But careful — should I check `final_url != url` too? Yes, in the 200 path.\n\nCareful with `HttpPage(429, \"\", b\"\", \"\")` — the transport returns it with final_url \"\". My orchestrator classifies status first. Good.\n\nHmm, one issue: `b\"<html>not json</html>\"` with content-type application/json (since url contains esearch.fcgi) → json parse fails → invalid_response. Good.\n\nTest: redirect detected even on 200:\n```python\ndef test_redirected_response_is_not_accepted(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    page = HttpPage(200, \"application/json\", _search_page(1, 0, 1, [\"111\"]), \"https://elsewhere.example/\")\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", transport=Pages([page]), clock=_clock)\n    assert result.status == \"invalid_response\"\n    assert not result.pagination_complete\n```\nGood — this covers the \"禁重定向\" contract at the receipt level.\n\nTest: loop guard.\n\n```python\ndef test_repeated_search_page_never_ends_as_completion(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([\n        _search_page(4, 0, 1, [\"111\"]),\n        _search_page(4, 1, 1, [\"111\"]),\n    ])\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", page_size=1, transport=pages, clock=_clock)\n    assert result.status == \"incomplete\"\n    assert not result.pagination_complete\n    assert [record.pmid for record in result.records] == []\n    assert len(result.search_pages) == 2  # partial evidence is retained\n    assert len(pages.urls) == 2           # the cursor never loops forever\n```\n\nAnd cursor mismatch:\n```python\ndef test_search_cursor_must_echo_the_request(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([\n        _search_page(2, 0, 1, [\"111\"]),\n        _search_page(2, 0, 1, [\"222\"]),\n    ])\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", page_size=1, transport=pages, clock=_clock)\n    assert result.status == \"invalid_response\"\n    assert not result.pagination_complete\n```\n\nHmm, wait. In this test, page 2 echoes retstart=0 but we requested 1 → invalid_response. Good.\n\nTest: empty search.\n\n```python\ndef test_authoritative_empty_search_is_not_a_failure(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([_search_page(0, 0, 200, [])])\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", transport=pages, clock=_clock)\n    assert result.status == \"no_records\" and result.pagination_complete\n    assert result.total_count == 0 and result.records == ()\n    assert result.universe_closed is False\n    assert len(result.search_pages) == 1 and not result.record_pages\n    assert ContentAddressedStore(tmp_path).read_bytes(result.search_pages[0].raw_asset) == _search_page(0, 0, 200, [])\n    assert len(pages.urls) == 1  # 无记录时不发起记录获取\n```\n\nTest: bad XML / missing records.\n\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize((\"body\", \"expected\"), [\n    (b\"<PubmedArticleSet><broken\", \"invalid_response\"),\n    (b\"<eFetchResult><ERROR>Invalid uid</ERROR></eFetchResult>\", \"invalid_response\"),\n    (b'<?xml version=\"1.0\"?><PubmedArticleSet></PubmedArticleSet>', \"incomplete\"),\n])\ndef test_record_document_faults_are_never_no_records(tmp_path, body, expected) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([_search_page(1, 0, 1, [\"111\"]), body])\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", page_size=1, transport=pages, clock=_clock)\n    assert result.status == expected\n    assert not result.pagination_complete\n    assert result.records == ()\n```\nHmm, careful: for the `incomplete` case, `total_count` is 1 (search succeeded) and pagination_complete False. Good.\n\nAlso: a partial efetch (2 requested, 1 returned) → incomplete with the partial record retained:\n```python\ndef test_partial_record_page_is_incomplete_not_complete(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([_search_page(2, 0, 2, [\"111\", \"222\"]), _records_xml(\"111\")])\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", transport=pages, clock=_clock)\n    assert result.status == \"incomplete\"\n    assert not result.pagination_complete\n    assert [record.pmid for record in result.records] == [\"111\"]\n```\nGood — \"保留部分证据\".\n\nTest: distinct exception types from the real download (monkeypatched opener).\n\n```python\nclass _Opener:\n    def __init__(self, error: Exception) -> None:\n        self.error = error\n\n    def open(self, request: object, timeout: float) -> object:\n        raise self.error\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize((\"error\", \"expected\"), [\n    (URLError(TimeoutError(\"timed out\")), PubMedTimeoutError),\n    (TimeoutError(\"timed out\"), PubMedTimeoutError),\n    (URLError(\"connection refused\"), PubMedNetworkError),\n    (OSError(\"broken pipe\"), PubMedNetworkError),\n])\ndef test_download_converts_transport_faults_to_distinct_typed_errors(\n    monkeypatch: pytest.MonkeyPatch, error: Exception, expected: type[Exception],\n) -> None:\n    monkeypatch.setattr(pubmed_fetch, \"build_opener\", lambda handler: _Opener(error))\n    with pytest.raises(expected):\n        pubmed_fetch._download(\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi\", 5.0, 1024)\n```\n\nHmm, `_download` signature `(url, timeout, max_bytes)`. Good. But monkeypatch lambda: `build_opener(handler)` is called as `build_opener(_NoRedirect())` → one positional arg. Good.\n\nAnd the HTTP error page is never persisted:\n```python\ndef test_download_never_returns_a_server_error_body(monkeypatch) -> None:\n    error = HTTPError(\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi\", 429, \"Too Many Requests\", {}, None)\n    monkeypatch.setattr(pubmed_fetch, \"build_opener\", lambda handler: _Opener(error))\n    page = pubmed_fetch._download(\"https://eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/entrez/eutils/esearch.fcgi\", 5.0, 1024)\n    assert page.status == 429 and page.body == b\"\"\n```\nHmm, HTTPError's constructor: `HTTPError(url, code, msg, hdrs, fp)`. `error.close()` is called in `_download`. HTTPError.close() works even with fp=None? `HTTPError.close()` → `self.fp.close()` if fp is not None... Actually `HTTPError.close()` is defined as:\n```python\ndef close(self):\n    if self.fp:\n        self.fp.close()\n```\nYes, guarded. OK.\n\nAnd the distinct HTTP-status exception types:\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize((\"status\", \"expected\"), [\n    (429, PubMedRateLimitedError),\n    (401, PubMedAccessDeniedError),\n    (403, PubMedAccessDeniedError),\n    (503, PubMedServerError),\n    (302, PubMedHttpError),\n])\ndef test_http_statuses_map_to_distinct_exception_types(status: int, expected: type[Exception]) -> None:\n    with pytest.raises(expected):\n        pubmed_fetch._classify_status(status, context=\"检索\")\n```\nNeed to import PubMedHttpError too.\n\nTest: query validation.\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"query\", [\"\", \"   \", \"x\" * 4001, \"bad\\x00term\"])\ndef test_invalid_query_is_rejected_before_any_request(tmp_path: Path, query: str) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([_search_page(1, 0, 1, [\"111\"])])\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, query, transport=pages, clock=_clock)\n    assert pages.urls == []\n```\nHmm, `pytest.raises(ValueError)` — the fetch function raises ValueError for invalid input (not a fetch failure). Good. And no request is made.\n\nAlso invalid limits:\n```python\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"overrides\", [\n    {\"page_size\": 0}, {\"page_size\": 10001}, {\"max_pages\": 0}, {\"timeout\": 0},\n    {\"max_page_bytes\": 0}, {\"max_total_bytes\": 0}, {\"efetch_batch_size\": 0},\n])\ndef test_invalid_limits_are_rejected(tmp_path, overrides) -> None:\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", transport=Pages([]), clock=_clock, **overrides)\n```\nHmm, `Pages([])` with no items → if validation fails first, no `next()` call. Good. But mypy isn't run on tests. Fine. Hmm, `**overrides` with dict[str, int] → runtime fine.\n\nTest: byte budget exhausted → incomplete, no truncated save:\n```python\ndef test_byte_budget_exhaustion_keeps_partial_evidence(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([\n        _search_page(2, 0, 1, [\"111\"]),\n        _search_page(2, 1, 1, [\"222\"]),\n    ])\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", page_size=1, max_total_bytes=len(_search_page(2, 0, 1, [\"111\"])), transport=pages, clock=_clock)\n```\nHmm, budget = exactly one page's size → first page consumes it, second page gets remaining = min(max_page_bytes, 0) = 0 → ≤ 0 → incomplete \"预算已耗尽\". Good:\n```python\n    assert result.status == \"incomplete\"\n    assert len(result.search_pages) == 1\n    assert len(pages.urls) == 1\n```\nHmm, is that too fiddly? It's a real requirement (\"预算\"). Keep.\n\nAlso max_pages exhaustion:\n```python\ndef test_page_budget_exhaustion_is_incomplete(tmp_path) -> None:\n    pages = Pages([_search_page(4, 0, 1, [\"111\"]), _search_page(4, 1, 1, [\"222\"])])\n    result = fetch_pubmed_results(tmp_path, \"term\", page_size=1, max_pages=2, transport=pages, clock=_clock)\n    assert result.status == \"incomplete\"\n    assert len(result.search_pages) == 2\n    assert len(pages.urls) == 2\n```\nGood: 2 pages allowed, count=4, so after page 2 (offset=2, collected 2 < 4) we need page 3 → budget exhausted → incomplete.\n\nHmm, careful with my loop structure: I check `page_number > max_pages` at the top of each iteration. Let me use a `for page_number in range(1, max_pages + 1)` like ctgov and return incomplete after the loop. That's cleaner and matches ctgov. Then after the loop → finish(\"incomplete\", \"页数预算已耗尽；保留部分证据并等待恢复\").\n\nNow the esearch loop and then efetch. Let me structure the code:\n\n```python\ndef fetch_pubmed_results(...):\n    # validation\n    download = transport or _download\n    store = ContentAddressedStore(project_root)\n    search_pages: list[CapturedResponse] = []\n    record_pages: list[CapturedResponse] = []\n    pmids: list[str] = []\n    total: int | None = None\n    byte_count = 0\n    acquired_at = _aware_clock(clock)\n\n    def finish(status, diagnostic):\n        return PubMedFetchResult(\n            query=query, status=status,\n            pagination_complete=status in {\"complete\", \"no_records\"},\n            total_count=total, records=tuple(records.values()),\n            search_pages=tuple(search_pages), record_pages=tuple(record_pages),\n            acquired_at=acquired_at, diagnostic=diagnostic,\n        )\n```\nHmm, `records` dict needs to be defined before finish. And for `no_records` raised inside the loop, records is empty. OK.\n\nCareful: `finish` uses `total` which is a closure variable — in Python, closures read the current value; since I reassign `total` inside the loop, `finish` sees the latest. Yes (no `nonlocal` needed for reading).\n\nLoop:\n\n```python\n    offset = 0\n    for page_number in range(1, max_pages + 1):\n        remaining = min(max_page_bytes, max_total_bytes - byte_count)\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            return finish(\"incomplete\", \"获取字节预算已耗尽；必须恢复，不能认定检索完成\")\n        url = build_pubmed_term_search_url(query, retstart=offset, retmax=page_size)\n        try:\n            response = download(url, timeout, remaining)\n            _classify_status(response.status, context=\"PubMed 检索\")\n            if response.final_url != url:\n                raise PubMedMalformedResponseError(\"接口状态或重定向不符合限定来源合同\")\n            if len(response.body) > remaining:\n                return finish(\"incomplete\", \"响应超出获取预算；未保存截断正文\")\n            if response.content_type.split(\";\", 1)[0].strip().lower() != \"application/json\":\n                raise PubMedMalformedResponseError(\"来源未返回JSON；不接纳错误页作为检索结果\")\n            acquired = _aware_clock(clock)\n            page = _parse_search_page(response.body, offset=offset)\n        except PubMedEmptyResultError as error:\n            raw = store.put_bytes(response.body, media_type=\"application/json\")\n            search_pages.append(CapturedResponse(page_number=page_number, request_url=url, acquired_at=acquired, raw_asset=raw, pmids=()))\n            total = 0\n            return finish(\"no_records\", error.diagnostic)\n        except PubMedFetchError as error:\n            return finish(error.status, error.diagnostic)\n        except OSError:\n            return finish(\"network_error\", \"公开接口网络获取失败；不是无数据\")\n        ...\n```\nProblem: `acquired` is assigned inside the try; if an exception occurs before, the except branch referencing `acquired` is a problem. In the EmptyResultError branch, `acquired` is assigned before `_parse_search_page` (which raises Empty). But if `_aware_clock` raises ValueError... that propagates (fine, a config error).\n\nHmm, but mypy will complain: \"possibly undefined\" variable? mypy doesn't track that for closures... Actually mypy does flag \"Cannot determine type of acquired\"? Let me structure it to avoid the issue: compute `acquired = _aware_clock(clock)` before the try block? But then a failed page would still have a clock reading — harmless. Hmm, but the empty-page capture needs it. Let me just compute `acquired` right after the download succeeds, before the try? Hmm, the download is inside the try.\n\nCleaner structure: separate the download+validate into a helper `_acquire_page(...)` that returns (response, acquired) or raises. Hmm.\n\nLet me restructure: \n\n```python\n        try:\n            response = download(url, timeout, remaining)\n        except PubMedFetchError as error:\n            return finish(error.status, error.diagnostic)\n        except OSError:\n            return finish(\"network_error\", \"公开接口网络获取失败；不是无数据\")\n        try:\n            _classify_status(response.status, context=\"PubMed 检索\")\n            if response.final_url != url: raise ...\n            ...\n        except PubMedFetchError as error:\n            return finish(...)\n```\nThat's two try blocks — acceptable and clear. Then inside the second try, `acquired` is defined before the parse call. The `except PubMedEmptyResultError` handler references `acquired`, which mypy considers defined (it's assigned earlier in the same try block). Hmm, mypy may still complain \"possibly unbound\"? mypy generally doesn't do that analysis for locals assigned before the raising call in the same block. Actually mypy does NOT implement possibly-undefined checks by default (that's pyright). Fine.\n\nLet me simplify further: split the \"save + parse\" into a small helper that returns the parsed page, and handle the empty case in the main flow:\n\n```python\n        try:\n            _classify_status(response.status, context=\"PubMed 检索\")\n            ...\n            page = _parse_search_page(response.body, offset=offset)\n        except PubMedFetchError as error:\n            if isinstance(error, PubMedEmptyResultError):\n                ... # unreachable? \n```\nNo. Keep two except clauses: `except PubMedEmptyResultError` first, then `except PubMedFetchError`. That's the standard pattern. Good.\n\nActually, hmm, an even simpler idea to avoid the awkward `except PubMedEmptyResultError` in the middle: since `_parse_search_page` raises Empty when count == 0, I can instead have `_parse_search_page` RETURN a page with `total=0, pmids=()` and have a separate tiny check. But then PubMedEmptyResultError has no raise site...\n\nOK, alternative raise site that's natural: the *efetch* phase. When the search found records but efetch returns zero articles → that IS a source anomaly. Hmm, but \"empty result\" for a fetch means the source returned no records — which the honest response is \"incomplete\", not \"no_records\".\n\nFine — keep `PubMedEmptyResultError` from `_parse_search_page` with the dedicated except clause. It's explicit and well-commented. Moving on.\n\nThen:\n\n```python\n        raw = store.put_bytes(response.body, media_type=\"application/json\")\n        search_pages.append(CapturedResponse(page_number=page_number, request_url=url, acquired_at=acquired, raw_asset=raw, pmids=page.pmids))\n        byte_count += len(response.body)\n        if total is not None and total != page.total:\n            return finish(\"incomplete\", \"检索期间来源总量变化，需重新核查集合\")\n        total = page.total\n        fresh = [pmid for pmid in page.pmids if pmid not in seen]\n        if page.pmids and not fresh:\n            return finish(\"incomplete\", \"来源重复返回同一分页游标；防止循环及虚假完成\")\n        seen.update(fresh)\n        pmids.extend(fresh)\n        if not page.pmids:\n            if len(pmids) != total:\n                return finish(\"incomplete\", \"来源声明总数与返回标识不一致；不能认定检索完成\")\n            break\n        offset += len(page.pmids)\n        if len(pmids) >= total:\n            break\n    else:\n        return finish(\"incomplete\", \"页数预算已耗尽；保留部分证据并等待恢复\")\n```\nWait, `for ... else` executes else when the loop completes without break. Yes. But careful: `return finish(...)` inside the loop body doesn't trigger else. Good.\n\nHmm, `if not page.pmids` when total > 0 → but _parse_search_page raises Empty when total == 0, and if total > 0 with empty idlist → that's the \"总数与标识不一致\" case. Let me handle: \n\n```python\n        if not page.pmids:\n            if len(pmids) != total:\n                return finish(\"incomplete\", \"来源声明总数与返回标识不一致；不能认定检索完成\")\n            break\n```\nIf total > 0 and idlist empty → len(pmids) < total → incomplete. Correct. If total == 0 → EmptyResultError already raised (so unreachable here). Hmm, then `len(pmids) != total` with total==0 and pmids==[] would be False → break → then post-loop verification... Let me simplify: since total==0 raises Empty, `not page.pmids` implies total > 0 and len(pmids) != total → always incomplete. So:\n\n```python\n        if not page.pmids:\n            return finish(\"incomplete\", \"来源声明总数与返回标识不一致；不能认定检索完成\")\n```\nCleaner. But wait — could a legitimate esearch page be empty while more pages exist? With retstart beyond the end, idlist is empty. E.g., count=2, we got 2 → we break before requesting. So no. Good.\n\nAfter the loop (break taken):\n```python\n    if len(pmids) != total:\n        return finish(\"incomplete\", \"来源声明总数与返回标识不一致；不能认定检索完成\")\n```\nHmm, if we broke because `len(pmids) >= total`, then len == total. If we broke because idlist empty, we returned. So this check is redundant... but it's cheap and defensive. Hmm, \"avoid over-engineering\". Let me keep it simple: after the break, verify `len(pmids) == total`; if not → incomplete. It's 2 lines and guards a real drift case. Actually if I break on `len(pmids) >= total`, and count changed... I check `total != page.total` per page, so drift is caught. And `len(pmids) > total` can't happen if each page adds fresh ids and we break at >=. Hmm, it can: count=2, page_size=2, page returns 3 ids → len(pmids)=3 > total=2 → break → len != total → incomplete. Good, so the check IS reachable. Keep it.\n\nThen the efetch phase:\n\n```python\n    records: dict[str, PubMedRecord] = {}\n    for start in range(0, len(pmids), efetch_batch_size):\n        batch = tuple(pmids[start:start + efetch_batch_size])\n        remaining = min(max_page_bytes, max_total_bytes - byte_count)\n        if remaining <= 0:\n            return finish(\"incomplete\", \"获取字节预算已耗尽；必须恢复，不能认定检索完成\")\n        url = build_pubmed_records_url(batch)\n        try:\n            response = download(url, timeout, remaining)\n        except PubMedFetchError as error:\n            return finish(error.status, error.diagnostic)\n        except OSError:\n            return finish(\"network_error\", \"公开接口网络获取失败；不是无数据\")\n        try:\n            _classify_status(response.status, context=\"PubMed 记录\")\n            if response.final_url != url:\n                raise PubMedMalformedResponseError(\"接口状态或重定向不符合限定来源合同\")\n            if len(response.body) > remaining:\n                return finish(\"incomplete\", \"响应超出获取预算；未保存截断正文\")\n            if response.content_type.split(\";\", 1)[0].strip().lower() not in {\"application/xml\", \"text/xml\"}:\n                raise PubMedMalformedResponseError(\"来源未返回XML；不接纳错误页作为论文记录\")\n            acquired = _aware_clock(clock)\n            batch_records = _parse_record_page(response.body)\n        except PubMedFetchError as error:\n            return finish(error.status, error.diagnostic)\n        returned = {record.pmid for record in batch_records}\n        if le